The problem requires calculating the total time John spends caring for 10 dogs, with each dog requiring 0.5 hours of attention per day.

**Step-by-step reasoning:**

1. **Daily time per dog:** Each dog takes 0.5 hours per day.
2. **Total daily time for all dogs:** 
   $$
   10 \text{ dogs} \times 0.5 \text{ hours/day} = 5 \text{ hours/day}
   $$
3. **Weekly time:** Assuming a 7-day week, multiply daily time by 7 days:
   $$
   5 \text{ hours/day} \times 7 \text{ days/week} = 35 \text{ hours/week}
   $$

Thus, the total number of hours John spends taking care of dogs in one week is $\boxed{35}$. 

