Now, he needs to remove 15 pounds in total. So if the comic books are already contributing 7.5 pounds, then the remaining weight he needs to remove from the toys is 15 minus 7.5. Let me subtract that: 15 - 7.5 equals 7.5 pounds. So he needs to remove 7.5 pounds worth of toys.

Each toy weighs 1/2 pound. To find out how many toys he needs to remove to get 7.5 pounds, I should divide 7.5 by 1/2. Dividing by a fraction is the same as multiplying by its reciprocal, so 7.5 divided by 1/2 is 7.5 multiplied by 2. That gives me 15. So, he needs to remove 15 toys.

