When Freda cooks canned tomatoes into sauce, they lose half their volume. Each 16 ounce can of tomatoes that she uses contains three tomatoes. Freda’s last batch of tomato sauce made 32 ounces of sauce. How many tomatoes did Freda use?

So, the key points here are:

1. When Freda cooks canned tomatoes into sauce, they lose half their volume. That means that the volume of the sauce is half the volume of the original tomatoes. So if she starts with, say, V ounces of tomatoes, after cooking, she ends up with V/2 ounces of sauce.

2. Each 16-ounce can of tomatoes contains three tomatoes. So, each can has 3 tomatoes, and the can is 16 ounces.

3. Freda's last batch made 32 ounces of sauce. We need to find out how many tomatoes she used.

